id: flow-of-combat
name: Flow of Combat
order: 5
category: mind
importance: secondary
description: >
  You are as serene and peaceful in combat as you are at a tea party, graceful and poised even in the midst of battlefield chaos.
text: >
  Flow of Combat (Mind): You are as serene and peaceful in combat as you are at a tea party, graceful and poised even in the midst of battlefield chaos.
  (1)-[Triggered]: If you suffer no Damage from an Opponent’s Attacking Maneuver that targets you, this triggers your Exploit Maneuver.
  (2)-[Triggered/Start of Turn]: If you have taken no Damage since the end of your last turn, you may use Combat Recovery as if you spent 1 Action as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. If you do, ignore the reduction to your Defense Value from the effects of Combat Recovery.
  (3)-[Triggered, 1/Encounter]: If you are targeted by an Opponent’s Attacking Maneuver, you may use the Defend Maneuver without spending a Counter Action.

---

# (1) The Exploit Maneuver offered on the attack's card at the one who made it, when it left you without Damage - yours
# to take (chat.mjs offerFlowExploit).
# (2) At the start of your turn with no Damage taken since the end of your last, Combat Recovery offered out of sequence,
# as if for 1 Action, its Defense Value not lost (chat.mjs flowOfCombatTurnStart).
[passive]
allow exploit.onNoDamage;
allow combatRecovery.flowOfCombat;

# (3) Ticked in Respond as you Defend: no Counter Action for it.
[triggered/defending, 1/encounter]
defend.free = true;
